  "goodToKnow": "Die Dämmerung is twilight, both dusk (Abenddämmerung) and dawn (Morgendämmerung). Dämmern means to grow dark or light, and figuratively, es dämmert mir means it's dawning on me. Wagner's opera Götterdämmerung (Twilight of the Gods) ends his Ring cycle, and the word entered English. Animals active at twilight are dämmerungsaktiv. Plural: die Dämmerungen."
